            "tool_p2": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Food safety isn't only about one temperature. SafeCook™ measures what matters: the total time spent at bacteria-destroying temperatures. 165°F is the instant-kill number on the chart. The USDA's full standard counts time at temperature, and chicken held at 150°F for about 4 minutes is just as safe, and a lot more delicious. SafeCook does that math for you and tells you the moment your food clears it.</p><p>There's a faster version for thermometer owners as well. Start around 300°F, then step the oven down as the surface temperature approaches your target. It's the same low-and-slow result, about 30% faster.</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
