                          "type": "text",
                          "settings": {
                            "text": "<p><strong>Serves</strong> 8 to 12<br><strong>Prep</strong> 24 hours to 3 days<br><strong>Cook</strong> 5 to 7 hours</p><ol><li><strong>Dry brine.</strong> At least 12 hours before roasting, heavily salt the turkey. Don't worry about overdoing it: there is a limit to how much salt can dissolve into water, and excess salt just sits on the surface. Blend in additional seasonings with the salt to suit your taste. Refrigerate on a wire rack, uncovered, for at least 12 hours. After 12 hours, brush off any remaining salt and let it air dry in the fridge for up to 3 days.</li><li><strong>Preheat the oven</strong> to 250°F (120°C) for convection, or 275°F (135°C) for non-convection.</li><li><strong>Truss.</strong> Remove the wishbone from the turkey to make carving easier, and truss the turkey.</li><li><strong>Insert the thermometer and add the elixir.</strong> Insert the Combustion Predictive Thermometer into the thickest part of the breast. Brush the bird with the Golden Brown Turkey Elixir if you want it to look perfect.</li><li><strong>Cook low and slow</strong> until the core reaches 155°F (68°C). Expect 4 to 5 hours for a 12-pound (5.4kg) bird.</li><li><strong>Rest</strong> for at least 30 minutes, but several hours is fine. The surface will cool, but the interior will still be hot enough to serve.</li><li><strong>Crisp the skin.</strong> Increase the oven temperature to 500°F (260°C). Brush on more elixir if you're using it, and then crisp and brown the skin for 5 to 10 minutes.</li><li><strong>Divide and conquer.</strong> The breast meat is juicy and ready to serve, but the legs and thighs are going to be tough, so separate the crown and return the dark meat to the oven until it reaches at least 170°F (77°C), about 15 to 20 minutes. Be sure to drop the oven back to 400°F (205°C) to avoid smoking up your kitchen.</li><li><strong>Carve and enjoy.</strong></li></ol>",
                            "width": "100%",
                            "max_width": "none",
                            "alignment": "left",
                            "type_preset": "rte",
                            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                            "font_size": "1rem",
                            "line_height": "normal",
                            "letter_spacing": "normal",
