                "recipe_sub_1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p><strong>Choosing your target temperature</strong></p><p>White and dark meat are at their best at different doneness temperatures, so choose your target based on what matters most to you. Is the juiciest white meat the priority? Follow the recipe as written, and return the dark meat to the oven while you carve the breast, to bring it up to at least a tender 170°F (77°C).</p><p>Don't care as much about perfect white meat, and don't want to take that extra step? Set the thermometer to 170°F (77°C). If you've brined the bird, it'll still be plenty juicy throughout.</p>",
