              },
              "blocks": {
                "faq_1": {
                  "type": "_accordion-row",
                  "settings": {
                    "heading": "Can I make this without the thermometer?",
                    "open_by_default": false,
                    "icon": "none",
                    "width": 20
                  },
                  "blocks": {
                    "faq_1_a": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>The recipe is written around temperatures, not times, so it needs a leave-in thermometer of some kind. A basic probe gives you the core temperature. The Predictive Thermometer adds the countdown to when the bird will be ready, the surface reading that the faster version depends on, and SafeCook.</p>",
                        "width": "100%",
                        "max_width": "none",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "rte",
                        "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                        "font_size": "1rem",
                        "line_height": "normal",
                        "letter_spacing": "normal",
                        "case": "none",
                        "wrap": "pretty",
                        "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color8 }}",
                        "background": false,
                        "background_color": "#00000026",
                        "corner_radius": 0,
                        "padding-block-start": 0,
                        "padding-block-end": 0,
                        "padding-inline-start": 0,
                        "padding-inline-end": 0
                      },
                      "blocks": {}
                    }
                  },
                  "block_order": [
                    "faq_1_a"
                  ]
                },
                "faq_2": {
                  "type": "_accordion-row",
                  "settings": {
                    "heading": "Where does the probe go in a turkey?",
                    "open_by_default": false,
                    "icon": "none",
                    "width": 20
                  },
                  "blocks": {
                    "faq_2_a": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>A turkey has a cavity in the middle, so don't aim for the center. Go for the thickest part of the breast, past the minimum insertion line and away from the bone. Breast and thigh finish at different times, so a whole turkey is the classic case for two thermometers: one in the breast and one in the thigh.</p>",
                        "width": "100%",
                        "max_width": "none",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "rte",
                        "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                        "font_size": "1rem",
                        "line_height": "normal",
                        "letter_spacing": "normal",
                        "case": "none",
                        "wrap": "pretty",
                        "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color8 }}",
                        "background": false,
                        "background_color": "#00000026",
                        "corner_radius": 0,
                        "padding-block-start": 0,
                        "padding-block-end": 0,
                        "padding-inline-start": 0,
                        "padding-inline-end": 0
                      },
                      "blocks": {}
                    }
                  },
                  "block_order": [
                    "faq_2_a"
                  ]
                },
                "faq_3": {
                  "type": "_accordion-row",
                  "settings": {
                    "heading": "Can I really cook it from frozen?",
                    "open_by_default": false,
                    "icon": "none",
                    "width": 20
                  },
                  "blocks": {
                    "faq_3_a": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>Yes. Start in a low oven, season the bird once the skin is wet to the touch, and put the thermometer in once the breast has thawed, about 2 hours in. From freezer to table takes about 5 hours.</p>",
                        "width": "100%",
                        "max_width": "none",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "rte",
                        "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                        "font_size": "1rem",
                        "line_height": "normal",
                        "letter_spacing": "normal",
                        "case": "none",
                        "wrap": "pretty",
                        "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color8 }}",
                        "background": false,
                        "background_color": "#00000026",
                        "corner_radius": 0,
                        "padding-block-start": 0,
                        "padding-block-end": 0,
                        "padding-inline-start": 0,
                        "padding-inline-end": 0
                      },
                      "blocks": {}
                    }
                  },
                  "block_order": [
                    "faq_3_a"
                  ]
                },
                "faq_4": {
                  "type": "_accordion-row",
                  "settings": {
                    "heading": "Which setup should I get?",
                    "open_by_default": false,
                    "icon": "none",
                    "width": 20
                  },
                  "blocks": {
                    "faq_4_a": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>The probe alone works with the free app. Add the WiFi Booster to check in from anywhere, or the WiFi Display if you'd rather glance at the counter than your phone.</p>",
                        "width": "100%",
                        "max_width": "none",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "rte",
                        "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                        "font_size": "1rem",
                        "line_height": "normal",
                        "letter_spacing": "normal",
                        "case": "none",
                        "wrap": "pretty",
                        "text_color": "{{ settings.color_palette.color8 }}",
                        "background": false,
                        "background_color": "#00000026",
                        "corner_radius": 0,
                        "padding-block-start": 0,
                        "padding-block-end": 0,
                        "padding-inline-start": 0,
                        "padding-inline-end": 0
                      },
                      "blocks": {}
                    }
                  },
                  "block_order": [
                    "faq_4_a"
                  ]
                },
                "faq_5": {
                  "type": "_accordion-row",
                  "settings": {
                    "heading": "Do I need my phone?",
                    "open_by_default": false,
                    "icon": "none",
                    "width": 20
                  },
                  "blocks": {
                    "faq_5_a": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>Not necessarily. The probe works with the free Combustion app on iOS, Android, macOS and watchOS, or you can read the countdown off the WiFi Display and leave the phone alone.</p>",
                        "width": "100%",
                        "max_width": "none",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "rte",
                        "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
